01:14:28,580 --> 01:14:30,140
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: 800 pesos

656
01:14:30,140 --> 01:14:32,180
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: yung powdered na UBE.

657
01:14:32,660 --> 01:14:35,180
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: May pondo na kaming gagamitin

658
01:14:35,180 --> 01:14:36,240
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: for 2026

659
01:14:36,240 --> 01:14:38,620
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: from sarili namin.

660
01:14:38,760 --> 01:14:40,720
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Then 2027, mas malaki pang pondo.

661
01:14:41,140 --> 01:14:43,360
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So eventually, doon sa mga small farmer,

662
01:14:43,440 --> 01:14:44,820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: pamimigayin natin yung seedlings.

663
01:14:45,180 --> 01:14:46,620
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Oo, kasi natanong ko yan.

664
01:14:47,780 --> 01:14:48,980
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Nakikita ko yung yield

665
01:14:48,980 --> 01:14:50,260
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: per hectare.

666
01:14:50,880 --> 01:14:51,520
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Napakaganda.

667
01:14:52,460 --> 01:14:55,960
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kung umaani ng 25 tons,

668
01:14:56,860 --> 01:14:58,380
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: napakalaking halaga ng pera.

669
01:14:58,380 --> 01:14:59,660
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kung susumayin natin.

670
01:15:00,080 --> 01:15:02,660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tama ho kayo, ma’am.

671
01:15:03,100 --> 01:15:03,920
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Nakita ko siya eh.

672
01:15:04,500 --> 01:15:05,800
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kaya in-encourage ko sila.

673
01:15:05,940 --> 01:15:07,980
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Ako, diyan na kayo magtanim kaysa naman sa iba pa.

674
01:15:09,120 --> 01:15:14,080
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Ang problema nga, Mr. Secretary, yung seedlings, talagang medyo bitin.

675
01:15:14,340 --> 01:15:17,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, yung head dyan, si Yusek Yang.

676
01:15:18,060 --> 01:15:21,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At papakordinate ko na sa office niyo para masigurado.

677
01:15:21,560 --> 01:15:29,860
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kasi yung Isabela, pinakoconvert namin halos na magtanim nila ng ube kaysa naman yung iba pa.

678
01:15:30,840 --> 01:15:33,560
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kasi pag kinuwenta mo yung halaga, talagang napakalaki.

679
01:15:35,300 --> 01:15:37,820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero kailangan lang violet talaga yung ube.

680
01:15:37,840 --> 01:15:41,380
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yung violet na yung pinakamagandang klase, hindi ho ba ang daming klase yan?

681
01:15:42,080 --> 01:15:47,940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron na kami na piling limang variants na po, yung napapromote natin.

682
01:15:47,940 --> 01:15:51,960
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Oo, yung sa bayan namin sa Jones, Isabela, ang ganda ng klase ng ube.

683
01:15:52,780 --> 01:15:59,940
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Eh, bagamat, yung nga, pag gustuhin mo ma magtanim, kasi 25,000 seedlings ang dapat itanim para mas...

684
01:16:00,840 --> 01:16:02,940
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mas maganda, ani per hektar.

685
01:16:03,900 --> 01:16:04,320
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Hindi po ba?

686
01:16:05,120 --> 01:16:09,060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pinadala nila ako ng samples na may picture ako.

687
01:16:09,480 --> 01:16:11,460
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Oo, ganda, ganda ho yun.

688
01:16:11,900 --> 01:16:12,200
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Sige.

689
01:16:12,420 --> 01:16:15,140
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At saka napakalaking demand nung ube talaga.

690
01:16:34,170 --> 01:16:35,910
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Nintay lang ho natin si chairman.

691
01:16:36,710 --> 01:16:40,170
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Siya ho yung may last parting words sa atin.

692
01:27:17,660 --> 01:27:18,000
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Representative.

693
01:27:19,560 --> 01:27:20,680
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: From minority.

694
01:27:22,320 --> 01:27:24,000
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Representative Sara Ilago.

695
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:26,740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair.

696
01:27:26,920 --> 01:27:33,280
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nais kong magtanong tungkol sa implementasyon ng Executive Order No. 100

697
01:27:33,280 --> 01:27:40,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sa pagtitiyak na magkakaroon tayo ng pag-establish ng floor price ng palay

698
01:27:40,180 --> 01:27:50,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at magkaroon ng nantiyak na suporta sa ating mga magsasaka sa panahon na napakataas po ng cost of production

699
01:27:50,960 --> 01:27:53,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at iba pang mga factors na nakakaapekto.

700
01:27:54,000 --> 01:27:56,240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa pagbagsak ng presyo ng palay.

701
01:27:59,190 --> 01:28:07,830
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, if I recall, yung EO 100 was sa pag-ano ng floor price sa pagbili ng, I think, government, no?

702
01:28:07,950 --> 01:28:13,630
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And it's sa presyo ng palay, no?

703
01:28:14,210 --> 01:28:19,590
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Oo, at yun nga, yun nga, yung ano na yun is limited to government

704
01:28:19,590 --> 01:28:24,630
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at hindi siya pwede i-apply sa private sector, Mr. Chair.

705
01:28:26,270 --> 01:28:29,370
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pagkano ho ang presyo na na-establish ninyo?

706
01:28:30,090 --> 01:28:36,330
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa ngayon, ang NFA is we are buying now set ang palay at wet ng 21.

707
01:28:37,290 --> 01:28:41,390
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa dry naman, 25 to 27, depende sa area.

708
01:28:41,770 --> 01:28:44,010
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pesos per kilo, Mr. Chair.

709
01:28:46,830 --> 01:28:51,430
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa budget nyo ho ba, saan po nakapaloob yung mga kinakailangan na pondo

710
01:28:51,430 --> 01:28:54,410
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para matiyak na nagtatrabaho ang ating steering committee,

711
01:28:54,410 --> 01:28:57,430
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na gagawa ng DA ang kanyang responsibilidad?

712
01:28:58,250 --> 01:28:59,130
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ang pondo, sorry.

713
01:28:59,130 --> 01:28:59,790
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Matiyak ito.

714
01:29:00,250 --> 01:29:03,650
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, ang pondo natin sa pagbili ng palay ay nasa NFA

715
01:29:03,650 --> 01:29:08,710
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at meron pa tayong rise for all na 10 billion.

716
01:29:09,450 --> 01:29:12,390
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa NFA is 9 billion pambili.

717
01:29:12,630 --> 01:29:14,390
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa rise for all is 10 billion.

718
01:29:14,530 --> 01:29:21,690
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So, total of 19 billion ang pondong pwedeng magamit sa 2026 sa pagbili ng palay, Mr. Chair.

719
01:29:21,690 --> 01:29:25,130
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pwede ho kayong mag-ulat dito sa Section 3,

720
01:29:25,570 --> 01:29:28,230
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: yung pagkakaroon ng temporary storage ng palay.

721
01:29:28,250 --> 01:29:33,250
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa public facilities, meron na ho ba tayong mga nakatulungan ng mga NGAs

722
01:29:33,910 --> 01:29:39,430
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at iba't ibang instrumentalities nito, GOCCs, LGUs,

723
01:29:39,610 --> 01:29:41,790
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: pati na rin state universities and colleges,

724
01:29:42,370 --> 01:29:47,350
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: meron ho ba tayong mga nahikayat, mga naisama sa pagtitiyak na

725
01:29:47,350 --> 01:29:51,130
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: meron ho silang mga facilities na maaari nating magamit

726
01:29:51,130 --> 01:29:53,190
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: bilang temporary storage ng palay?

727
01:29:54,450 --> 01:29:57,250
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Maybe we can ask NFA to continue.

728
01:29:57,250 --> 01:29:57,970
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: To continue.

729
01:29:58,250 --> 01:29:59,990
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Initially, Madam Ms.

730
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:03,400
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, sa ngayon, medyo mas maganda

731
01:30:03,400 --> 01:30:05,480
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: sitwasyon natin compared to last year

732
01:30:05,480 --> 01:30:10,760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: dahil ang ating NFA last year same time

733
01:30:10,760 --> 01:30:12,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ay punong-puno lahat ng palay.

734
01:30:13,380 --> 01:30:16,200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa ngayon, ang i-report ni ng NFA

735
01:30:16,200 --> 01:30:18,660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: kung ilan percent na na pero di hamak na

736
01:30:18,660 --> 01:30:19,500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: mas mababa ngayon.

737
01:30:19,600 --> 01:30:22,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ready tayo ngayon mag-accept ng bagong palay

738
01:30:22,160 --> 01:30:25,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: not like last year sa same period.

739
01:30:25,680 --> 01:30:28,400
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pangalawa, meron din mga LGUs na tumutulong

740
01:30:28,400 --> 01:30:30,600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: sa atin like ang Pampanga LGU

741
01:30:30,600 --> 01:30:31,920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: although nabinaha sila ngayon.

742
01:30:32,420 --> 01:30:35,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron silang bagong malalaking warehouse facility

743
01:30:35,880 --> 01:30:37,960
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: na papagamit din sa NFA.

744
01:30:38,480 --> 01:30:41,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ang Isabela meron din and other LGUs

745
01:30:41,440 --> 01:30:42,660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: among others.

746
01:30:43,040 --> 01:30:47,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: I would like NFA Admin Larry to add to this,

747
01:30:47,240 --> 01:30:47,640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair.

748
01:30:50,050 --> 01:30:50,930
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

749
01:30:51,070 --> 01:30:52,370
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Tama po si Secretary.

750
01:30:53,110 --> 01:30:56,670
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: May mga LGUs na nakatulong po sa atin

751
01:30:56,670 --> 01:30:58,230
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: sa pagpapahiram ng kanilang bodega.

752
01:30:58,230 --> 01:30:59,690
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Nabanggit niya po ang Pampanga,

753
01:30:59,970 --> 01:31:02,270
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: nandyan din po ang NFA Isiha.

754
01:31:02,850 --> 01:31:05,570
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: I think sa Kabanatuan yata yun,

755
01:31:05,790 --> 01:31:09,770
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: yung malaking area for storage.

756
01:31:09,990 --> 01:31:12,690
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: So yun po yung mga nakatulong sa atin.

757
01:31:12,870 --> 01:31:15,730
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Pagdating naman po sa kahandaan

758
01:31:15,730 --> 01:31:17,670
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: na meron tayong pag-iimbakan

759
01:31:17,670 --> 01:31:19,050
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: ngayong darating na anihan,

760
01:31:19,630 --> 01:31:22,150
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: in fact, na-free up na natin

761
01:31:22,150 --> 01:31:23,690
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: ang more than 40%

762
01:31:23,690 --> 01:31:25,530
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: ng ating mga bodega.

763
01:31:25,530 --> 01:31:29,950
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Kasama na rito yung mga pinakinuhan ating mga private,

764
01:31:29,970 --> 01:31:32,030
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: private warehouses na re-rentahan.

765
01:31:32,470 --> 01:31:34,290
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: At patuloy pa tayong nag-free up

766
01:31:34,290 --> 01:31:36,210
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: ng ating mga warehouses

767
01:31:36,210 --> 01:31:37,710
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: para nang sa gayon.

768
01:31:38,430 --> 01:31:41,090
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Marami po pwedeng pag-iimbakan ng ani

769
01:31:41,090 --> 01:31:44,070
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: dito sa darating na anihan.

770
01:31:44,910 --> 01:31:46,970
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, pagdating sa funding requirement,

771
01:31:47,850 --> 01:31:49,010
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang sabi dito sa EO,

772
01:31:49,270 --> 01:31:52,330
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kukunin po ito sa pondo ng DA,

773
01:31:52,550 --> 01:31:54,970
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: dun sa kanilang mga existing na appropriations

774
01:31:55,670 --> 01:31:58,310
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ng DA at ng iba pang constraint agencies.

775
01:31:58,850 --> 01:31:59,910
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Magkano po ba ang nag-iimbakan?

776
01:31:59,910 --> 01:32:00,710
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Magkano ba na-gastos ninyo

777
01:32:00,710 --> 01:32:02,930
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: mula nang mailabas itong EO na ito

778
01:32:02,930 --> 01:32:06,230
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: from October 2025 hanggang ngayon?

779
01:32:06,610 --> 01:32:08,670
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At sinabi rin dito, Mr. Chair,

780
01:32:08,790 --> 01:32:11,410
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na kung kailangan na magkaroon ng pondo

781
01:32:11,410 --> 01:32:12,810
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa susunod na taon

782
01:32:12,810 --> 01:32:14,910
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ay responsibilidad ng concerned agencies

783
01:32:15,530 --> 01:32:16,910
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na mag-propose

784
01:32:17,470 --> 01:32:18,970
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kung ano ho yung kailangan nila.

785
01:32:19,370 --> 01:32:20,830
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, magkano ho ang nag-gastos

786
01:32:20,830 --> 01:32:23,530
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: mula 2025 at meron bang proposal

787
01:32:23,530 --> 01:32:25,310
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa susunod na taon?

788
01:32:28,220 --> 01:32:31,320
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Mr. Chair, pagdating sa EO na yan,

789
01:32:31,920 --> 01:32:38,460
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: ang pondo lamang po ni NFA na nakukuha sa national government is 9 billion.

790
01:32:39,200 --> 01:32:43,100
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: So yan po yung ginagasos natin since January.

791
01:32:43,780 --> 01:32:47,420
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: So kung ano man po yung pondo na nagamit doon,

792
01:32:47,480 --> 01:32:51,180
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: yun lamang po ang pwedeng ma-attribute dyan po sa EO na yan.

793
01:32:51,300 --> 01:32:53,980
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Pero pagdating po sa DA, funding ng DA na kung saan,

794
01:32:54,720 --> 01:32:57,220
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: sabi nyo nga po, kukuhaan din doon yung ibang mga pondo.

795
01:32:58,220 --> 01:32:59,540
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Hindi po tayo aware doon.

796
01:32:59,600 --> 01:33:01,600
NFA Administrator Larry R. Lacson: Ang aware po tayo doon sa NFA funding.

797
01:33:02,680 --> 01:33:07,800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung sa Mr. Chair, yung sa DA fund naman may dagdag pan 10 billion na hindi pa nagagamit.

798
01:33:08,600 --> 01:33:11,680
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At gagamitin natin ngayong harvest season na ito,

799
01:33:11,800 --> 01:33:17,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: yung remaining funds ng NFA plus yung 10 billion for the Rice for All program, Madam Chair.

800
01:33:18,280 --> 01:33:24,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: What about Mr. Chair, yung sinabi ko ng NFA na magre-renta tayo ng mga private warehouses.

801
01:33:24,360 --> 01:33:26,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Magkano po ang kinakailangan para dyan?

802
01:33:27,480 --> 01:33:31,720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At hindi po ba tayo magkakaroon ng mas pinalakas na kampanya

803
01:33:31,720 --> 01:33:37,860
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: doon sa mga nabanggit ko kanina from other NGAs, LGUs, GOCCs,

804
01:33:37,940 --> 01:33:42,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: even state universities and colleges na maaari po natin paggamitan ng public facilities

805
01:33:42,960 --> 01:33:47,500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para mabawasan naman ho yung gastos natin para sa private warehouses?

806
01:33:48,100 --> 01:33:52,080
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Just, Mr. Chair, basically ganito, no?

807
01:33:52,900 --> 01:34:01,360
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung dating capacity ng NFA when I became Secretary was only 450,000 tons of palay.

808
01:34:01,720 --> 01:34:10,340
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa ngayon, marami na tayo natapos na warehouse sa funding nung 2024 GA and 2025 GA

809
01:34:10,340 --> 01:34:16,720
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: na ang ngayon ang capacity natin is from 500,000 tons, naging 800,000 tons natin.

810
01:34:17,660 --> 01:34:17,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tama?

811
01:34:18,640 --> 01:34:24,100
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So 800,000 tons na yung internal capacity ng NFA lang yun.

812
01:34:24,660 --> 01:34:28,660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Plus nag-renta pa tayo ng mga warehouses plus yung warehouses sa iba.

813
01:34:28,660 --> 01:34:31,480
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: With the amount of money we have now,

814
01:34:31,720 --> 01:34:40,680
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: enough na yung space na capacity natin, base sa buying quantity.

815
01:34:40,900 --> 01:34:42,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tapos meron pa tayong programa ngayon.

816
01:34:42,680 --> 01:34:50,000
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Dati kasi ang problema, hindi tayo makapaglabas ng bigas or palay dahil kung walang kalamidad.

817
01:34:50,600 --> 01:34:56,760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ngayon meron tayong 20 bigas ng ating 20 peso rice natin.

818
01:34:56,760 --> 01:34:59,780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At tuloy-tuloy na ang benta nun, araw-araw.

819
01:35:00,360 --> 01:35:00,760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And we're talking about...

820
01:35:01,720 --> 01:35:09,540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: 20,000 to eventually 40,000 tons a month yun na tuloy-tuloy lumalabas habang bumili-bili tayo.

821
01:35:09,660 --> 01:35:14,200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So we are in a better, much, much better position now than before, Mr. Chair.

822
01:35:15,480 --> 01:35:21,360
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, tungkol naman sa implementation ng Executive Order No. 101,

823
01:35:21,680 --> 01:35:29,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: nakadikit itong EO-100 na nag-tutulakho ng full implementation ng Sagipsaka Act.

824
01:35:29,960 --> 01:35:31,700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So magkaugnay po yung dalawang yan.

825
01:35:31,720 --> 01:35:39,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At nais natin ma-require talagang government entities kasama ng LGUs na bumili ng food supplies,

826
01:35:39,780 --> 01:35:46,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: agricultural products na diretsyo mula sa mga farmers and fisher folk cooperatives.

827
01:35:46,880 --> 01:35:52,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At dinedirekta din ito sa ilalim ng batas na ito na magkaroon tayo ng mga Sagipsaka desk.

828
01:35:52,700 --> 01:35:56,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Magkano ho ba ang gagastusin dito ng DA para sa susunod na taon?

829
01:35:56,560 --> 01:35:58,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At kung maaari din kayong mag-ulat.

830
01:35:59,000 --> 01:36:00,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kumusta ho ba yung sitwasyon?

831
01:36:01,720 --> 01:36:04,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pagdating sa pagtitiyak, halimbawa dito sa Kongreso,

832
01:36:05,380 --> 01:36:09,360
